---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Panel from '../components/Panel.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/url';
import { readLastRun, freshness } from '../lib/state';
import { sourceLabel } from '../lib/record';

const lastRun = readLastRun();
const fresh = freshness(lastRun);
const sources = Object.entries(lastRun?.sources ?? {});
---

<Base
  title="About — IEA Wind Data Catalogue"
  description="How the IEA Wind Data Catalogue is built: aggregation only, provenance on every field, and no registration."
>
  <div class="prose stack-6">
    <h1>How this works</h1>

    <p>
      Nobody who has already described a dataset on Zenodo is going to log into a
      second system and describe it again. So this catalogue does not ask them
      to. It watches the places IEA Wind people already publish and reflects what
      it finds.
    </p>

    <h2>What it does</h2>
    <p>
      A scheduled job reads seven sources — Zenodo, DataCite, Crossref, GitHub,
      OSTI, the Wind Data Hub and iea-wind.org — and writes what it finds into an
      append-only event log. The records you see are derived from that log and
      regenerated from it; delete them and they come back byte for byte.
    </p>

    <h2>What it will not do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>It never edits a source.</strong> If a Zenodo record has a typo'd
        title, then a typo'd title is what Zenodo says, and the fix belongs at
        Zenodo — where the author can make it and every other consumer benefits.
        Every record carries a link to report an issue at its source.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>It never accepts an identifier from a model.</strong> Where a
        page has to be read by a language model, identifiers are extracted by
        pattern and resolved against DataCite or Crossref before the record
        exists. A DOI that does not resolve is dropped and logged.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>It never mirrors a file.</strong> Metadata and links only. The
        availability badge on each record says plainly whether the files are open,
        restricted, embargoed or behind a registration wall.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>It never deletes a record.</strong> When something vanishes
        upstream the page stays, with a notice, so existing citations keep
        resolving. Link rot is the failure mode a catalogue exists to fight.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Provenance</h2>
    <p>
      Every field records how it was known: read from an API, matched by pattern,
      or inferred by a model. Machine-inferred fields carry a violet badge with
      the model and its confidence, everywhere on the site. Being honest about
      which metadata is inferred is the difference between a catalogue people
      trust and one that gets dismissed the first time somebody spots a
      confidently wrong abstract.
    </p>

    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      Corrections are additive and local: a curator can attach a note, add a Task
      attribution, or link a related record, but the upstream value keeps being
      displayed verbatim beside the note. Both truths on the page.
    </p>

    <h2>Machine access</h2>
    <p>
      Every record page carries schema.org <code>Dataset</code> JSON-LD, so the
      catalogue is indexable by Google Dataset Search. The whole catalogue is
      also published as <a href={withBase('/catalog.jsonld')}>DCAT</a>, and the
      underlying records are CKAN <code>package</code> dicts — the format a CKAN
      instance would ingest unmodified, should there ever be a reason to run one.
    </p>

    <h2>The last run</h2>
    {fresh.neverRun ? (
      <Panel tone="info" icon="ℹ">
        <p>No run report in this checkout yet.</p>
      </Panel>
    ) : (
      <>
        <p>
          Harvest {lastRun?.harvest_version} finished {fresh.finishedAt}, wrote{' '}
          {lastRun?.records?.written ?? 0} record
          {lastRun?.records?.written === 1 ? '' : 's'} and appended{' '}
          {lastRun?.events_appended ?? 0} event
          {lastRun?.events_appended === 1 ? '' : 's'}.
        </p>
        {sources.length > 0 && (
          <table class="sources scroll-x">
            <caption class="visually-hidden">Per-source result of the last harvest</caption>
            <thead>
              <tr><th scope="col">Source</th><th scope="col">Seen</th><th scope="col">Changed</th><th scope="col">State</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {sources.map(([name, result]) => (
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row">{sourceLabel(name)}</th>
                  <td>{String(result.seen ?? 0)}</td>
                  <td>{String(result.changed ?? 0)}</td>
                  <td>
                    {result.implemented === false
                      ? 'not implemented'
                      : result.reachable === false
                        ? 'unreachable'
                        : 'ok'}
                  </td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        )}
      </>
    )}
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .sources {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: var(--font-size-small);
  }

  .sources th,
  .sources td {
    padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-3);
    border-bottom: var(--border-width-hairline) solid var(--border-subtle);
    text-align: start;
  }

  .sources thead th {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-caption);
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  ul {
    padding-inline-start: var(--space-4);
  }

  li + li {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-3);
  }
</style>
